-- Present Perfect / Present Perfect Continuous --
We have been testing new functionality without interruption since Monday. - OR - We’ve been testing new functionality since Monday.
I have been learning English since September.
The bug has appeared since the last update. - OR- The bug has been present since the last update. (-the best for the Bug report).
The bug has been appearing since the last update. - Грамматически верно, но в QA-английском звучит не совсем естественно. - has been appearing → звучит так, будто баг появляется и исчезает (обычно мы фиксируем факт существования бага).
We have been working on this bug since this morning.
  Use Present Perfect Continuous to describe ongoing processes.
Use Present Perfect to state the existence or result of a bug.
